            <div xml:id="d81">

                <pb facs="0136" n="64" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg64"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 14716/2–3.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Consul Pontius to the
                            Assistant Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Consulate General</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-06-26"><hi rendition="#italic">June 26,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 177.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to state that with further
                    reference to my No. 175, dated June 19, 1908, on the subject of the status of
                    the Tai Hong Co., I inclose herewith copy of reply of legation to my dispatch
                    forwarded to it. The legation’s instructions will be complied with and the
                    present inclosure is forwarded to the department in the hope that same will
                    prove of assistance should the department wish to instruct this consulate in the
                    matter also.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Albert W.
                    Pontius.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d81-a1.xml" xpointer="d81-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
